"answer": "The Q2 budget has undergone several revisions and updates based on recent performance and project outcomes. Initially, the profit forecast for Q2 was revised to $9.378 million, reflecting a 3.5% increase from previous estimates, with funds shifted toward emerging market bonds (content:04). However, capital expenditure projects, including the new office building construction and IT infrastructure upgrade, came in 10% over budget, necessitating further adjustments to financial projections to cover these overages (content:06). Additionally, an unplanned IT expenditure of $50,000 for new security software was identified, which will also impact the Q2 budget and requires approval (content:01). These changes are being prepared for a routine financial audit scheduled for the second week of next month (content:05)."
